# 🌐 Google Cloud Vertex AI Multimodal Integration (`gcp-vertex-multimodal-integration`)

## When to Use
Use when wiring local prototypes, Electron/Tauri apps, or backend services to generate text, tool calls, images, video, voiceovers, music, or transcripts using the user's active Google Cloud Account (`Vertex AI` & `Cloud APIs`) instead of paid third-party API keys (OpenAI, ElevenLabs, Runway, Decart, Suno).

Also use when installing and building foreign Node/Electron/Swift repositories in `../DNK_Vibe/` while reusing shared system environments (`pnpm` store, `uv`) without creating redundant virtual environments.

---

## 🔑 1. Active Google Cloud Account & Token Discovery (Zero Manual Keys)

1. **Project ID Discovery Order**:
   - Read `.dnk_active_project.env` in `DNK_HUB` root (`CLOUDSDK_CORE_PROJECT` / `GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT`, currently `project-2826e39f-abdc-4c1d-8b5` for `devagent.dnk@gmail.com`).
   - Fallback to `process.env.GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT || process.env.CLOUDSDK_CORE_PROJECT`.
   - Fallback to `gcloud config get-value project`.
2. **OAuth2 Bearer Token Minting**:
   - **Direct ADC Refresh (Zero Daemons / Node & Electron Plugins)**: Read `~/.config/gcloud/application_default_credentials.json` and exchange `refresh_token` with `https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token` (`grant_type=refresh_token`). Fast (~200ms) and requires no external CLI process.
   - **CLI Fallback with Path Probing**: In macOS desktop/Electron environments, `process.env.PATH` is minimal. Probe `/opt/homebrew/bin/gcloud`, `/usr/local/bin/gcloud`, and `~/google-cloud-sdk/bin/gcloud` before executing `gcloud auth print-access-token`.
   - Run `gcloud auth print-access-token` or `gcloud auth application-default print-access-token` and cache in-memory for ~45 minutes.
   - Always pass `Authorization: Bearer <TOKEN>` and `x-goog-user-project: <PROJECT_ID>`.
   - **Never** combine `x-goog-api-key` with `Authorization: Bearer` on `aiplatform.googleapis.com` (causes HTTP 401).

